s one it  sure got a melancholy vibe but its story  is packed with plenty of charm and jokes  that balance its tone you play as a crow  whose job is to collect souls and  honestly it's kind of a grind in a nine  to five kind of way however when an  elderly crow steals one of your souls  well you're forced to cross a land of  devoid of death to get it back you'll be  hacking slash and dodging and shooting  your way through tough bosses and some  unruly characters it's a cool spin on  the soulsborne gameplay loop made  popular by from software games but a  little more approachable it's also got  the yi ol familiar ghibli inspiration to  tout  [Music]  a legendary addition for a legendary  franchise  whether you're playing it all over again  or this is your first time the mass  effect legendary edition is mass effect  1 2 3 wrapped up and remastered so take  control of commander shepard and strap  in for galactic adventure across the  milky way set in the 22nd century where  choices matter and span across all three  games besides there's another mass  effect on the way so here's a pretty  compelling reason to explore this  bioware classic  speaking of trilogies the hitman trilogy  is now on game pass 2 become the iconic  bald guy with the barcode on the back of  his head and enter an intricate world of  assassination this is the pinnacle of  the hitman franchise and has some of the  best levels and locations to play over  and over again because getting the lay  of the locations learning the routines  of your targets and exploring the many  many ways in which you can assassinate  someone is nothing short of just  remarkable game design and this trilogy  is the shining achievement of developer  io interactive it'll also make you  realize why there's probably no better  developer suited for james bond games so  here's looking forward to whatever  they're doing with that  you know what maybe investing yourself  into a sprawling trilogy set in space or  being a cool bald ag